          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it safe for children to wear perfume?",
            "answer": "In general, yes, as long as it is gentle and used lightly. Alcohol-free body mists sprayed onto clothing rather than skin are the safest option for children. Always patch test something new first, and if your child has sensitive skin, eczema or allergies, check with your paediatrician before use."
