        "faq3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "At what age can a child start wearing perfume?",
            "answer": "There is no fixed rule, but gentle, alcohol-free mists are commonly used from around school age, applied lightly to clothing. For younger children and babies, it is best to avoid fragrance on the skin and to speak with your paediatrician first."
